# settings.json and settings2.json are hand-compacted on purpose: the permission
# allow-lists are grouped by stack on single lines so they read as a table. Prettier's
# defaults would expand each into ~60 lines, turning any one-line edit into an
# unreviewable diff. Prettier is not part of the quality gate (§19.3), so it has no
# business rewriting them. The hooks/format.sh PostToolUse hook honors this file, so
# editing either settings file no longer triggers a reformat. Everything else
# (Markdown, and real code in repos that use this config) is still formatted normally.
settings.json
settings2.json
